.TH ZIPROJ 1 "2026-10-08" "ziproj 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ziproj \- zip a project to share with an AI assistant or a colleague, without secrets or build junk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ziproj
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-r ]
.RB [ \-a ]
.RB [ \-f ]
.RB [ \-x
.IR pattern ]...
.RB [ \-o
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-gitleaks ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-open ]
.RI [ directory ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ziproj
creates
.IR name .zip
from
.I directory
(the current directory by default), where
.I name
is the directory's name.
It leaves out files that commonly hold secrets and files that only add weight,
then scans what is left for secrets before writing anything.
.PP
The steps, in order:
.IP 1. 4
List the files.
Inside a git repository the list comes from
.BR "git ls-files" ,
so
.I .gitignore
is honoured, untracked files that are not ignored are included,
and submodules are followed.
In a folder that is not a repository, each nested repository is listed
through git and everything else through
.BR find (1).
.IP 2. 4
Zip the list into a private temporary folder, applying the default exclusions,
the ignore files and the
.B \-x
patterns.
Symbolic links are stored as links and never followed.
.IP 3. 4
Scan exactly what is in the zip for secrets: built-in patterns, plus
.BR gitleaks (1)
when it is installed.
.IP 4. 4
If secrets are found, stop (default), or replace them with
.B REDACTED
inside the zip
.RB ( \-r )
and scan again to verify.
.IP 5. 4
Only when everything passed, move the zip to the output folder and reveal it
in Finder (macOS) or the file manager (Linux desktop).
.PP
Your files are never modified.
A zip left over from an earlier run is deleted at the start of every run that
writes, so a blocked or failed run never leaves a stale zip to upload by mistake.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
List what would be zipped and scan it.
Nothing is written.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-redact
Replace each detected secret with
.B REDACTED
inside the zip instead of blocking.
Private key blocks become
.BR REDACTED\-PRIVATE\-KEY .
A value found in one file is also replaced in every other file that contains it.
The redacted files are scanned again; anything still detected blocks the zip.
With gitleaks installed this option needs
.BR jq (1).
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-ai
AI mode: also leave out images, PDFs, fonts, audio, video and design files,
which an AI assistant reading code does not need.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-exclude " \fIpattern\fR"
Leave out a file, a directory or a glob, at any depth.
A leading
.B /
anchors the pattern to the project root.
Can be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-out " \fIdir\fR"
Write the zip to
.IR dir .
The default is
.B $ZIPROJ_OUT
if set, otherwise
.IR ~/Downloads .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Write the zip even if secrets are still in plain text.
Prefer
.BR \-r .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-gitleaks
Do not use gitleaks, even if installed, and do not ask about it.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-open
Do not reveal the zip after writing it.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.PP
Short options can be bundled:
.B ziproj \-nra
is
.BR "ziproj \-n \-r \-a" .
.SH IGNORE FILES
Rules are read, in this order, from:
.TP
.I ~/.config/ziproj/ignore
Applies to every project.
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is honoured.
.TP
.IR directory /.ziprojignore
Applies to the project.
.TP
.IR repository /.ziprojignore
In each repository nested inside
.IR directory ,
relative to that repository.
.PP
One rule per line.
Blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
are ignored.
.TP
.I pattern
Exclude matching files and directories at any depth.
.B *
matches any characters, including
.BR / .
.TP
.I /pattern
Exclude only at the root of the folder that holds the ignore file.
.TP
.BI "noscan: " path
Keep
.I path
(a file or a directory) in the zip but skip the secret scan on it.
Use it for known false positives, such as test fixtures.
.SH DEFAULT EXCLUSIONS
Always left out, whether tracked by git or not.
Secret file and folder names are matched in any letter case.
.TP
Secrets
Environment files
.RI ( .env ", " .env.* ", " .envrc ),
credential files
.RI ( .netrc ", " .npmrc ", " .pypirc ", " .git\-credentials ),
keys and certificates
.RI ( *.pem ", " *.key ", " *.p8 ", " *.p12 ", " *.jks ", " *.keystore ),
provisioning profiles,
.IR GoogleService\-Info.plist ,
.IR google\-services.json ,
service account JSON files,
.IR Secret.* " and " Secrets.* ,
.IR local.properties ,
Terraform state and variables, local databases, and the
.IR .ssh ", " .aws ", " .gnupg ", " .docker ", " .kube
and
.I secrets
directories.
.TP
Weight
Version control data, dependencies
.RI ( node_modules ", " Pods ", " .venv ),
build output
.RI ( build ", " dist ", " .build ", " DerivedData ", " target ", " .next ),
caches, logs, OS litter
.RI ( .DS_Store ),
compiled objects, app packages
.RI ( *.ipa ", " *.apk ", " *.aab )
and archives.
.PP
The complete list is in the source and in the project documentation.
.SH SECRET SCANNING
The built-in patterns recognise private keys and common token formats
(AWS, Google, OpenAI, Anthropic, GitHub, GitLab, Slack, Stripe, SendGrid,
npm, Hugging Face, Azure, JWTs and database URLs with a password).
.PP
.BR gitleaks (1),
when installed, adds hundreds of rules and entropy checks, including generic
API keys.
If gitleaks is missing,
.B ziproj
explains the risk and asks before going on;
in a non-interactive shell it stops unless
.B \-\-no\-gitleaks
is given.
.PP
The project cannot switch the scan off: in the copy that gitleaks scans,
.I .gitleaks.toml
and
.I .gitleaksignore
files are removed,
.B gitleaks:allow
comments are defused and
.B GITLEAKS_CONFIG
is ignored.
Use
.B noscan:
rules for false positives.
.PP
Findings are printed as
.IR path : line ,
never with the secret value.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ZIPROJ_OUT
Default output folder.
.TP
.B ZIPROJ_NO_OPEN
Set to 1 to never reveal the zip.
.TP
.B ZIPROJ_GITLEAKS
Path or name of the gitleaks executable.
.TP
.B ZIPROJ_GITLEAKS_CONFIG
A gitleaks configuration file to scan with.
Without it gitleaks uses its default rules.
.TP
.B ZIPROJ_JQ
Path or name of the jq executable.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colours.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Location of
.IR ziproj/ignore .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The zip was written, or a dry run found no secrets.
.TP
.B 1
Secrets were found and nothing was written, the redaction could not be
verified, or an error occurred.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid options.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted (SIGINT).
.TP
.B 143
Terminated (SIGTERM).
.SH EXAMPLES
Zip the current project into
.IR ~/Downloads :
.PP
.RS
.B ziproj
.RE
.PP
See what would go in, without writing anything:
.PP
.RS
.B ziproj \-n
.RE
.PP
Share with an AI assistant: no media, secrets redacted:
.PP
.RS
.B ziproj \-ar ~/Code/my\-app
.RE
.PP
Leave out the store metadata and write to the desktop:
.PP
.RS
.B ziproj \-x fastlane/metadata \-o ~/Desktop
.RE
.SH CAVEATS
Scanning reduces risk; it cannot prove that a project is free of secrets.
A credential in a format that neither the built-in patterns nor gitleaks
recognise is zipped as is, with or without
.BR \-r .
Review the file list
.RB ( \-n )
before sharing anything sensitive, and keep secrets out of your repositories.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zip (1),
.BR git\-ls\-files (1),
.BR gitleaks (1),
.BR jq (1)
.PP
